  "query_preview": "/Tuesday through Saturday/... \nBy Tuesday, deep troughing and strong negative height anomalies \nwill amplify and intensify along the west coast, however \nconfidence in the timing and depth of this feature continues to be\nlow to moderate. The deterministic's have started to come into \nbetter agreement compared to 24 hrs ago but still show key \ndifferences. The ECMWF forecast continues to show a slightly \nslower system however much shallower than before. Meanwhile the \nGFS deterministic remains mostly unchanged, with the exception of \nnow leaning towards a more positively tilted trough than compared \nto the ECMWF, and the previous GFS runs, spreading out any \nvorticity advection and hindering better chances for storm \ndevelopment. Even with these differences compared to previous \nruns, the ECMWF continues to forecast a more more robust rainfall \nscenario in comparison to the GFS. Either way, Wednesday and \nThursday continue to be the best window for rainfall potential, \nwhile pattern recognition and some instability parameters suggest \nthe potential for strong thunderstorms ahead of the shortwave \npassage. Lingering PoPs continue into Friday morning before \nexpecting to dry out by the weekend. \n\nAdditionally, with the uncertainty of this next system remaining,\na wide spread in NBM temperatures continue throughout the week, \nmost notably on Thursday with a spread of 11 degrees between the \n25th and 75th percentile. Even with this large of spread below \nnormal highs are likely late this week heading into the weekend.",
